00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.450
A quick comedy

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.280
Acted out and welcomed with an encore

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.950
Teary goodbyes are fiction

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.360
Well, that's because those would be painful

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.530
I don't want that

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.690
Let's make a promise!

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.400
Let's make this a happy ending

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.530
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.070
Question, question, question,
question, question mark

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:19.400
Every, every, every, every, everyone

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.810
You're not picking on boys, are you?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.580
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!
Conch, conch, conch, conch shell

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.380
Conch, conch, conch, conch shell

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.710
Sounding, sounding, sounding,
sounding, sounding off

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:33.620
Let's gather, where should we meet?

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:36.890
Ra ta tat... Ra ta tat...

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.420
You are your own peak
Ra ta tat... Ra ta tat...

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.990
Climb a little and take a rest

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.900
Clothes for Saturday 398

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.690
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.490
February 10, Everywhere by Bicycle

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.670
Sae! Hiro!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:56.790
Come over here!

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.210
Where did you get that bicycle?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.310
A classmate gave it to us.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.550
What? Why?

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:13.990
She won a bicycle at a
department store lottery.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.820
She had an old one that she wasn't using.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.550
Oh? That's amazing!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.260
Let's use it together!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.060
Can I ride it?

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.360
Go right ahead.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:25.890
Squeak...

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.360
Squish...

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.700
I-It's not what you think.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.790
The tires are flat!

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.540
See? They are flat!

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.510
I'm glad we had an air pump.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.610
Yeah!

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.080
Completed!

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.280
Yuno, do you want to ride it next?

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.150
O-Okay!

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:51.910
Wobble

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.820
Stop

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.690
She looks like she wants help.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.030
Can't you ride a bike, Yunocchi?

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.330
Yeah, I can ride one.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:05.170
But it's been a while and I
can't get the knack of it.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.070
Then, let's practice!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.440
O-Okay!

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.640
Say, want to go down to the flood plain?

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.270
Ah, the flood plain.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:16.740
There's an exam going on now, and it
wouldn't be good if we made a lot of noise.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.720
Huh? Isn't that kind of far?

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.380
How far away is it?

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.950
20 minutes by bike.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.820
Does Hiro plan on riding down herself?

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.420
Is she still mad about earlier?

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.130
I see.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:36.530
The last time you rode a bike
was before you came here.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:38.440
You had one at your house, didn't you?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.910
Yes, I figured I wouldn't use it here,
so I left it behind.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.010
Me too.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:48.170
Speaking of bicycles, when I was younger,
I used to love letting go of the handle bars!

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.550
I could never do that. I rode normally.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.520
Sae, have you ridden a bike
with another person?

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.460
Yeah! I've ridden with another person!

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.160
I have bittersweet memories of how it felt
to have arms wrapped around my waist!

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.630
Around My

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.300
"Around my"?
Peddling with the weight of two
people felt very youthful.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.800
She was the one who was peddling.
Peddling with the weight of two
people felt very youthful.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:06.660
Peddling with the weight of two
people felt very youthful.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.540
Say, why don't we name the bicycle?

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.670
Name?

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:13.700
Let's see...

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.440
It moves around a lot.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.740
How about "Gofer"?

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:17.980
That's a little awkward...

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.470
What a low position.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.310
Then, how about "Director"?

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.110
Gofer

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:23.710
Director

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.690
The wind sure feels nice, doesn't it, Director?

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.380
Wait, Miya-chan!
Wait, Miyako!

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.580
Run, run!

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.460
Wow, it's really wide!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.030
It feels good!

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.830
Thank goodness, it's not too cold.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.570
It's been a while since I've been here.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:45.260
What's the name of this river?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.070
Peach
It's written as peach flower river
and called Touka River.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:46.670
Peach Flower
It's written as peach flower river
and called Touka River.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.440
Peach Flower River
It's written as peach flower river
and called Touka River.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.470
Class I River
Peach Flower River
It's written as peach flower river
and called Touka River.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.840
Oh?

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:57.140
That would mean that if a seal showed up in
this river, its name would be "Tou-chan."

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.540
Tou-chan...

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:02.650
Plop!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.390
That looks comfortable. I want to try that too!

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.820
Plop.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.930
The sky is so big.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.200
I can hear people playing baseball.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.560
It really feels wonderful.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.600
Wow! Amazing!

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.670
It's really high!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:21.710
Did you see that?

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.800
That was a true home run!

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:24.610
You're amazing, lady!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.800
Gone
You're amazing, lady!

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.880
Relax and slam it.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.880
Oh?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.540
Miya-chan is really into it.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.850
She looks like she's having fun!

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.390
I'm getting sleepy.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.220
Shall we get started?

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:43.490
Huh?

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.300
Y-You're right.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.500
I'll give it my best!

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.330
She completely forgot about it, didn't she?

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.610
You used to be able to ride before, right?

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.810
Yes, I used to be able to ride normally.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:02.680
Okay, then try to ride it with
that image in mind.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:03.580
Okay!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:03.850
Don't try so hard, and relax your shoulders!
Okay!

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.580
Don't try so hard, and relax your shoulders!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.350
Okay!

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:06.580
Believe in yourself.
Okay!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.480
Believe in yourself.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.350
Okay!

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:08.490
You can ride the bicycle.
Okay!

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.250
You can ride the bicycle.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.060
I can ride it!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:11.260
You can do it!
I can ride it!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.360
You can do it!

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:13.160
I can do it!

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:13.360
You won't give in!
I can do it!

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:14.460
You won't give in!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.530
I won't give in!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.690
Is this part of practice?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.160
I'll show you how it's done!

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:24.000
Watch closely, Yunocchi!

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.400
Miya-chan, watch where you're going!

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.380
Skiddddd...

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.850
That was close.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.020
I could never do that.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.220
Impossible...

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.360
Fight, Yunocchi!

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:56.160
I get the feeling that I'll be all
right if I can get peddling.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:57.820
I see...

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.140
Then, I'll hold you from the back.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.210
Try peddling as hard as you can.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.170
Okay!

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.870
You're going to release me, aren't you?

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.200
I see you already get the idea.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.220
This is a bit awkward.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.310
Getting older is depressing.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.820
It's not going well.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.560
Yeah, it feels strange.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.760
I wonder what it could be?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.420
Say, could it be?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.570
Did you get on it after running
beside it like this?

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:29.330
Oh!

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:29.570
Bingo?
Oh!

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:30.070
Bingo?

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:30.330
Bingo?
That's right, I had forgotten.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.530
That's right, I had forgotten.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.500
So, that's it? Is that all there was to it?

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:38.110
Hop Hop
Hop hop...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.340
Well, I'm glad we figured it out.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:41.810
Hop Hop
Hop hop...

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.910
Hop Hop
Hop hop...

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.620
That's odd.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.020
This is the way I got on it.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.090
Say...

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:55.830
Yes?
Say...

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.160
Perhaps you're standing on the wrong side.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.220
Hiro is left-handed,
so if you do the same thing...

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.640
I can ride it!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.280
I'm hungry!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:26.470
Me too.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:29.070
All right, it's all done!

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:31.150
Wow! It looks delicious!

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.170
It smells good!

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.950
Bon appétit!

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:38.420
It's hot, but delicious!

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:41.150
Miyako, try not to splash the soup.

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:45.160
During winter, you really feel like
eating curry udon, don't you?

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.560
It's really delicious!

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:50.120
Yeah, we were also hungry from walking a lot.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.570
I'm glad that we're all able to ride the bicycle!

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.510
Yeah!

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.870
How should we use it?

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:02.380
Perhaps we should use it
whenever we feel like it.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.540
Okay!

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:07.580
If we have something we need to do,
we should say something in advance.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.720
Got it.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:13.890
I'm glad that it will be easier when
I buy heavy things, like rice.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:16.330
It's also helpful when we go on outings.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.820
Or when we visit home.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.920
Your home is in Fukuoka.

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.700
Do you plan on crossing the
Kanmon Strait by bicycle?

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.540
Mind if I do that, Hiro?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.510
It's all right, I'm almost finished.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.070
Done.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.940
Say, what do they have in the afternoon?

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:38.720
For the entrance exam.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:40.720
If I'm not mistaken, the art department
has practical skills

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.910
and the liberal arts department
has interviews.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:47.450
I'm kind of curious, even though
we're not doing anything.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.230
Thank you for your help today.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:52.760
What's this about?

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:56.820
You ended up helping me out on a holiday.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:58.540
It's all right.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:03.210
It was very difficult to ride
a bicycle the first time.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.810
But I'm glad I got to ride it again today,
though not immediately.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:10.980
When did you first learn how to ride a bicycle?

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.070
When I entered elementary school.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.850
I was already able to ride it before
I entered elementary school.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.390
You're very athletic.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:20.950
I learned late.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.990
I finally began learning how
in the second grade.

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.800
It has nothing to do with athletic ability.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.930
I fell down a lot before I was able to ride it.

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:32.070
What about you, Miya-chan?

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:34.470
Umm, fifth Grade, I think.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.510
How unexpected, that's pretty late.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:40.740
My family only had adult bicycles.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.610
So, that's it.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.770
I suppose you couldn't ride those
when you were little.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:48.750
Oh?

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:49.820
Who could that be?

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:51.080
Coming!

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:52.960
Huh?

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.490
Sorry for coming over so suddenly.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:57.580
I'm Toudou of the Yamabuki High
School Broadcasting Club.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.160
Toudou?

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.830
Oh, the sportscaster for the
whole-team relay on field day!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.740
Yeah, she's the captain of
the Broadcasting Club.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.140
So, what did you want?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:12.040
I actually came to interview all of you
here at Hidamari Apartments.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:13.470
What?!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.440
I'm going to be graduating soon.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:24.190
I wanted to write my final broadcast
script for the new students.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:28.690
I wanted to write something that showed
how fun Yamabuki High School was.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.930
But everything I wrote ended up too serious.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:39.260
That's when I thought of doing
something on all of you.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:42.200
But why us?

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:47.440
Hidamari Apartments is famous for bringing
together eccentrics in the art department.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:49.680
Huh? Eccentrics?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.450
We're not...

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:52.780
We're normal.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:55.450
Some of our upperclassmen were
some real characters though.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.250
Yeah, like Misato Sempai.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.180
The person who graduated last year, right?

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.360
I've heard rumors about Misato Sempai.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.160
She left some devices that drop
washtubs from the ceiling of my room.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.030
What?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:08.300
I was surprised.
What?

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.670
I was surprised.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.930
But is's peaceful now, right?

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:15.710
Yeah, I got rid of the desiccant
packets in Miyako's room.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:16.870
Desiccant packets?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.830
There were lots of desiccant
packets under my flooring.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.510
My room leaks, so there was a risk
that they would catch fire.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:27.580
They didn't belong to Misato Sempai though.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.190
It was kind of scary during
the typhoon, wasn't it?

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:32.020
That happened, didn't it?

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.650
Hidamari Apartments truly is amazing.

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:37.290
Thank you very much.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:39.090
Huh? What about me?

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.230
Should we have talked about that?

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:45.620
Toudou was taking notes.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.430
Will that be useful to the new students?

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:50.340
Care for more tea?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:51.570
Oh, thanks.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.730
Grrrrrrowl

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:55.910
Hiro, I'm going to need some snacks soon.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:56.880
Miya-chan...

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:00.820
I don't have anything that will
be a good snack right now.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:03.220
What?! Hiro has no snacks?!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.190
I'm trying not to buy any.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.220
I end up eating them if I have them.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.430
Then, I'll go to Berima.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.830
Are you sure?

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.430
I wanted to look at some magazines.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.400
It will be really quick if I go by bike.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:16.630
It should take about a minute to get there.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.330
We're counting on you.

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.360
Okay!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.030
Oh...

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:26.880
The exams are over.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.670
Good work everyone.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.540
Natsume?

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.540
What's wrong?

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:38.180
Sae!

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.690
What are you doing?
We don't have school today.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:43.320
Did you go to school by mistake?

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:46.990
I-I came to school to help out with the exam!

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.820
Unlike you, I didn't laze around all day.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:52.400
So, what are you doing?

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.840
A girl dropped this by the
shoe compartments.

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:58.340
I tried to go after her, but I lost sight of her.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:00.840
She's probably already at the station.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.240
I see...

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:05.680
You should still be able to
catch up to her. Get on.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:06.650
What?!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:06.880
Quickly!
What?!

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:07.610
Quickly!

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.150
Hold on tight.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.070
Do you remember what she looks like?

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:29.860
Y-Yeah...

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.810
Someone beat me to it!

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.080
Shinya is headed to Fukuoka.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:37.110
That's amazing.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:42.250
If Shinya is going to go to Fukuoka by bike,
then I'll try to go to the United States!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.620
What?!

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:45.480
I wonder what happened to Sae?

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.720
I'm back.

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:49.330
Welcome back.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:50.830
Sorry I'm late.

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.020
I bought all sorts of things.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:55.200
Did something happen?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.970
I ran into Natsume by the school gates.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.030
Natsume?

00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:00.770
Are you going to open all of them up?

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:02.140
Can I?

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.840
Sure, let's eat it together.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:06.570
That's good, they all look delicious.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.550
I'm not sure how to rate them,
but I think this one is the best!

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.490
I'll have some too.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:20.220
So, what did you talk to Natsume about?

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.690
Did you fight again?

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:27.320
Just the usual stuff, but we wound up returning
something an exam student dropped.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.930
Is that so?

00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:31.370
The bicycle was a real help.

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.200
Oh?

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.040
Very good! I knew Director could do it.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.870
No! From now on, it's "President."

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:36.700
Director

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:37.500
President

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.010
It's been promoted again?

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.150
Thanks for your hospitality.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:44.610
Thanks for the food.

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:01.120
Ms. Yoshinoya!

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:04.430
Good evening.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.400
You seem tired.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:09.030
I'm not tired.

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:12.810
It's just that I was an examiner today.

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:16.810
I could sense how nervous all
of the exam students were.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:19.250
I feel relieved now that it's over.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:21.180
Is that so?

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:23.490
I think it would be great if we
could accept everyone

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:27.650
who wants to learn at Yamabuki High School.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:41.140
Good work, Ms. Yoshinoya.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.540
You can go home for today.

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:44.540
Okay!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:48.480
I wonder what encounters
we'll have this spring?

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.780
Spring is almost here, isn't it?

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:00.260
I see, we're going to have juniors soon.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.060
That sure was quick.

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:07.690
I wonder if we can treat our juniors the same
way that Sae and Hiro treated us?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.830
I think you'll be a good upperclassman.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:11.830
You think so?

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.370
I still can't believe it.

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:15.840
It hasn't hit me yet.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:20.240
I wonder if any first years will be
moving into Hidamari Apartments?

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.470
Who knows?

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:25.920
That's the door.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:27.040
Huh?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.950
Landlady!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.560
What's wrong?

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:36.820
Hey! I thought that I should
take these away already.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.360
What are those?

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.060
Want to try these out, Yuno?

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:43.570
If you want to use them,
I can leave them here.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.400
Please take them with you.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.000
Good evening.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:51.570
Hey! These things are really heavy.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:57.050
It's probably impossible to take
them away all at once.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.340
You think so too?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.340
Then, could you load some of them on that?

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:03.980
Huh?

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.590
Thanks, you're a great help.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.760
Landlady, I think there's still some left over.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.930
All that's left are the big ones.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.510
Is that Sae's bicycle?

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.240
No, we're all sharing it.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.280
Oh? Bicycles sure are great.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:33.680
They're eco-friendly, very eco-friendly.

00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:35.320
Yeah!

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:36.990
Can I ride it sometimes?

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:38.220
Sure!

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:39.890
Thanks!

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:43.290
Mopeds use up gasoline,
and I've always wanted a bike.

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:44.890
Huh?

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.160
Having a bike sure is convenient.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:54.030
Is the landlady going to make more
use of the bicycle than we are?

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.290
I'd like to go to the public bath.

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.150
I can get there quickly by bicycle.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:14.120
But I suppose it would be cold if I went by bike.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.060
I might catch a cold.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:18.250
What other places should I go to?

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.890
I know somewhere I want go by bicycle!

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:28.200
February 10 The End

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:32.310
One
One!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.210
One!

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:38.170
February 11, The Tortoise and the Hare

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:40.920
Miya-chan!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.280
Good morning!

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.120
'Morning!

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:44.050
Where's Yuno?

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:46.110
She left ahead of us by bicycle.

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:50.090
Her middle school didn't allow bicycles,

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:52.730
so she always dreamed of going
to school by bicycle.

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:54.160
I see.

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:57.330
Good morning!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.600
Huh? Where were you, Yuno?

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:02.500
I was chaining the bicycle to the bike rack.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:09.640
February 11, The End

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:25.390
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.390 --> 00:22:31.130
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:31.770 --> 00:22:38.170
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:43.980
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:50.050
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:55.620
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:57.230
Run all night

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:00.300
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:03.630
Your singing voice

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:06.700
Touches my heart

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:09.970
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:09.970 --> 00:23:13.110
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:16.310
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:19.750
Leads me through space

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:22.620
A song about shooting stars

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:26.160
I can't hear them

00:23:26.160 --> 00:23:30.090
I can't reach them

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.650
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:40.570 --> 00:23:41.970
Preview

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:45.270
Preview
Whenever it rains, I remember the drawing
song I used to sing when I was little.

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:47.380
Preview
My set square gets a crack in it.

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:49.040
Preview
Bread rolls and frogs show up.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:51.410
Preview
Come to think of it, it's an odd scene.

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:55.050
Preview
My mom made me put on a raincoat and boots.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:57.490
Preview
I had an umbrella and a handbag.
My hands were full.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:59.860
Preview
How nostalgic. What fond memories!

00:23:59.860 --> 00:24:02.560
Preview
I want to eat some fried dough!

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:05.830
Preview
The next episode is "June 6, Red String"

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:07.600
Preview
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments.

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:09.470
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:10.490
Preview
